1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:01,240
A trembling street.

2
00:00:01,465 --> 00:00:02,495
Rising water.

3
00:00:02,665 --> 00:00:03,575
Falling rock.

4
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:07,170
What turns a small movement
into a destructive force?

5
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:11,480
This street begins quietly.

6
00:00:12,315 --> 00:00:13,135
Then the ground shakes,

7
00:00:13,135 --> 00:00:17,065
while hanging lights and overhead
cables swing behind the motion.

8
00:00:18,150 --> 00:00:20,720
Below the surface,
a locked fault suddenly slips.

9
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:25,900
Released energy travels outward as seismic
waves through the surrounding rock.

10
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:30,340
Back above ground, buildings and loose
objects respond at different speeds.

11
00:00:31,145 --> 00:00:34,895
Dust escapes, fragments fall,
and weakened masonry breaks away.

12
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:38,560
In a separate ocean setting,
the seafloor suddenly rises,

13
00:00:38,770 --> 00:00:41,680
displacing the water above
it and starting long waves.

14
00:00:43,150 --> 00:00:47,260
Across deep water, a tsunami
carries energy over long distances.

15
00:00:48,410 --> 00:00:51,640
Approaching shallower water,
it slows and grows taller.

16
00:00:52,670 --> 00:00:55,410
The surge crosses the coast,
pours around buildings,

17
00:00:55,410 --> 00:00:57,620
and pushes a vehicle into the street.

18
00:00:58,355 --> 00:01:02,565
Floodwater spreads inland as its
forward motion gradually weakens.

19
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:09,140
On another hillside, rain enters the
soil and can reduce its strength.

20
00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:12,390
Cracks open as a mass begins to detach.

21
00:01:13,450 --> 00:01:15,480
Gravity accelerates the slide downhill.

22
00:01:15,735 --> 00:01:17,585
Large rocks bounce and rotate,

23
00:01:17,995 --> 00:01:20,625
while smaller fragments
and uprooted trees follow.

24
00:01:21,415 --> 00:01:23,465
Dust billows behind the moving material,

25
00:01:23,795 --> 00:01:26,525
then thins as debris
settles across the road.

26
00:01:30,150 --> 00:01:34,220
Volcanic gas expands and drives
ash and fragments from the vent.

27
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:37,950
Hot material rises into layered,
drifting clouds,

28
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:41,330
while heavier pieces follow
curved paths back down.

29
00:01:42,130 --> 00:01:44,860
Nearby, lava moves
slowly along the terrain.

30
00:01:45,125 --> 00:01:49,195
A dark crust forms above glowing channels,
warming the surrounding ground.

31
00:01:52,150 --> 00:01:55,620
These separate hazards reveal
how stored energy, gravity,

32
00:01:55,790 --> 00:01:58,280
and moving matter can
transform a landscape.

